  "answer_text": "It looks like there are several places called \"Glenwood Pool\"! Here's a summary of the most notable ones:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Resort \u2013 Glenwood Springs, Colorado\nThis is the world's largest hot springs pool! The resort has more than 7 expansive pools, including the original historic pool, and has been drawing visitors from all over the world since 1888. The source of the mineral water is the Yampah Spring, which produces over 3.5 million gallons of water per day at a temperature of 122\u00b0F. The Grand Pool contains over 1 million gallons of water and is an aquatic playing field for kids of all ages.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 2. Glenwood Pool \u2013 Forest Glen, Maryland\nGlenwood Pool is a swim club set back among the trees and along a creek in historic Forest Glen, Maryland. You can reach them at board@glenwoodpool.org for more information.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 3. Glenwood Houses Pool \u2013 Brooklyn, New York\nLocated in the Glenwood Houses neighborhood of Brooklyn, New York, this pool offers a place to cool off and enjoy the water during the hot New York summers. Managed by NYC Parks, it is a well-maintained facility that caters to the community's aquatic needs. It is located at Farragut Road & Ralph Avenue and can be reached at (718) 531-2480.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 4. Glenwood Springs Aquatic Center \u2013 Glenwood Springs, Colorado\nThis 277,000-gallon pool boasts 8 lap lanes and a one-meter diving board, ranging from 4 feet deep to 12 feet deep, with a temperature kept between 82\u201384 degrees. It is located at 100 Wulfsohn Road, Glenwood Springs, CO 81601.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfca 5. Glennwood Pool \u2013 Evans, Georgia\nGlennwood Pool is a non-profit, volunteer-run neighborhood pool in Evans, Georgia, offering memberships for residents and non-residents, seasonal events like dive-in movie nights, and military & senior discounts.\n\n---\n\nCould you let me know which **Glenwood Pool** you're interested in, or what city/state you're in? I can provide more specific information! \ud83d\ude0a",
